<%# What the load was applied TO.

    Two runs are only comparable if this matches, or differs on purpose. Shown
    from the first second of a run rather than only once it has been imported:
    it is fixed for the whole run — the runner refuses to switch the server
    while a test is measuring it — so there is nothing to wait for.

    Live, it comes from the run-config.txt the harness writes at launch; after
    import, from the row that recorded the same file. One source, read twice. %>

<h2>Server</h2>

<dl class="settings">
  <div>
    <dt>variant</dt>
    <dd><%= variant.presence || "server not recorded" %></dd>
  </div>
  <% if image.present? %>
    <div>
      <dt>image</dt>
      <dd><%= image %></dd>
    </div>
  <% end %>
  <% if settings.present? %>
    <div>
      <dt>settings</dt>
      <dd><%= settings.split(",").join(" · ") %></dd>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</dl>

<% if variant.blank? || variant == Run::UNKNOWN_VARIANT %>
  <p class="finding-body measure muted">
    This run does not name the server it measured, so it cannot be compared
    against one that does. Runs record it from
    <code>bin/campfire-variant</code> on the machine that generates the load;
    runs from before that, or taken while the deployed image did not match the
    recorded variant, say so here rather than guessing.
  </p>
<% end %>
